@startuml
' =====================================================================
' Analysis Class Diagram (BCE / robustness pattern = MVC)
' Logical View (4+1) - Elaboration phase (analysis) of RUP
' Scope: HU1-HU4 (section 2.3)
' ANALYSIS level: no types, no visibility (+/-/#), no exhaustive
' multiplicities. Focus on layer separation and relationships.
' =====================================================================

' --- project base style ---
allowmixing
' --------------------------------

title Analysis Class Diagram MVC — Version 2 with transitions - Selected User Stories (HU1–HU4)

' ====================== ACTORS ======================
actor "Business Administrator\n(Tenant)" as admin
actor "End Customer" as customer

' ============== VIEW LAYER (boundary) ============
package "Views (boundary)" {
  class TenantRegistrationView <<boundary>>
  class ScheduleConfigurationView <<boundary>>
  class CatalogManagementView <<boundary>>
  class PublicBookingView <<boundary>>
}

' =========== CONTROLLER LAYER (control) =========
package "Controllers (control)" {
  class TenantRegistrationController <<control>>
  class ScheduleConfigurationController <<control>>
  class CatalogManagementController <<control>>
  class PublicBookingController <<control>>
}

' ============ MODEL LAYER (entity) ================
' Names IDENTICAL to domain_model.puml (domain traceability).
package "Domain Model (entity)" {
  class Business <<entity>>
  class BusinessOwner <<entity>>
  class WorkingHours <<entity>>
  class Service <<entity>>
  class Employee <<entity>>
  class Customer <<entity>>
  class TimeSlot <<entity>>
  class Appointment <<entity>>
  class PendingAppointment <<entity>>
}

note top of Business
  Multitenant isolation: each business
  is a Tenant with its tenant_id; every
  query is filtered by that tenant_id (HU1).
end note

note bottom of PendingAppointment
  HU4 leaves the appointment in "Pending"
  state (Confirmed/Cancelled are out of
  scope: they belong to HU5 and later).
end note

' ============ ACTOR -> VIEW (boundary) =============
admin --> TenantRegistrationView
admin --> ScheduleConfigurationView
admin --> CatalogManagementView
customer --> PublicBookingView

' ============ VIEW -> CONTROLLER (control) ========
TenantRegistrationView ..> TenantRegistrationController
ScheduleConfigurationView ..> ScheduleConfigurationController
CatalogManagementView ..> CatalogManagementController
PublicBookingView ..> PublicBookingController

' ============ CONTROLLER -> MODEL (entity) ========
' HU1: business registration and tenant creation
TenantRegistrationController ..> BusinessOwner
TenantRegistrationController ..> Business

' HU2: schedule and working hours configuration
ScheduleConfigurationController ..> Business
ScheduleConfigurationController ..> WorkingHours

' HU3: catalog management (services and employees)
CatalogManagementController ..> Business
CatalogManagementController ..> Service
CatalogManagementController ..> Employee

' HU4: public appointment booking
PublicBookingController ..> Service
PublicBookingController ..> Employee
PublicBookingController ..> TimeSlot
PublicBookingController ..> Customer
PublicBookingController ..> Appointment

' ============ MODEL RELATIONSHIPS (domain) =======
' Labels in English; no multiplicities (analysis level).
BusinessOwner --> Business : owns
Business -- Employee : employs
Business -- Service : offers
Business -- WorkingHours : defines
Employee -- Service : is qualified for
WorkingHours -- TimeSlot : delimits availability of
Employee -- TimeSlot : is available in
Customer -- Appointment : books
Appointment -- Service : is for
Appointment -- Employee : is attended by
Appointment -- TimeSlot : occupies

' State relevant to HU4: the appointment stays Pending
Appointment <|-- PendingAppointment
@enduml
